  "section_notes": "The final S5 makes an 8-per-100k mandatory recall automatic with 24-hour notification after verification, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k). S2 sets a 5% threshold but removes any mandatory sales stop, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) since exceedance triggers only corrective action and regulator discretion. S3's 24-month new-unit delay (outside the ≤12-month acceptable band) and 6-year retrofit favour Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, and S4's 36-month suppression timing sits at Halcyon's HC-2 floor. The S2 5% threshold is described as 'under discussion', so its binding status is somewhat ambiguous, and the S5 notice figure is the 7-day general notice (the recall-linked notice is 24 hours)."
